# Abadis Med redesign — standing rules

## Git (two people + a team commit to this repo)
- Work ONLY on branch `siamak/redesign`. Start every task with `git fetch origin && git checkout siamak/redesign && git pull --no-rebase origin siamak/redesign`.
- Never push to `main`. Never `--force` / `--force-with-lease`. Never rewrite pushed history (no rebase/amend of pushed commits, no `reset --hard` onto remote work).
- ShushtarWolf and abadismedit also commit (e.g. branch `team-assets-*`). If the remote moved, MERGE (`git pull --no-rebase`); resolve conflicts keeping both sides' intent. Never overwrite or revert someone else's commit.
- Final delivery goes to `main` only through a Pull Request `siamak/redesign → main`, which a human merges. Do not merge it yourself.
- Small focused commits, message format `feat(site): …` / `fix(site): …` / `chore(tools): …` / `docs: …`.

## Generator vs hand-built pages
- Phase-2 pages are GENERATED by `python3 tools/redesign/build.py [group]` (groups: home products about dealers calculator csr contact customers experiences downloads install faq careers posts). Edit the Python in `tools/redesign/` and re-run; do not hand-edit their HTML in `site/`.
- Home (`site/index.html`) is generated by `pages_home.py` (Zagros hero + about / why / calculator / news / articles / customers). Hand-built pages: `site/products/suction-bag/index.html`. `site/csr/index.html` and `site/contact/index.html` are hand-built but the generator rewrites the blocks between `<!-- phase2:csr -->…<!-- /phase2:csr -->` / `<!-- phase2:contact -->…`. Shared header/footer on hand-built pages: `python3 tools/redesign/apply_shell.py`.
- Shared chrome (head, header, NAV, footer) lives in `tools/redesign/layout.py`. CSS: `site/assets/css/site.css`. JS: `site/assets/js/site.js`.
- `tools/build_site.py` is the LEGACY phase-1 generator — do NOT run it (it would overwrite home/suction-bag/csr/contact with the old 4-item nav).
- Images: `tools/redesign/data/imgmap.json` + raw cache `$ABADIS_IMG_RAW` (default `/workspace/abadis-wb/img-raw`, which does not exist on a PC). Re-running the generator without the raw cache would turn images into placeholders unless the cache fallback (prompt 0 in docs/cursor/CURSOR-PROMPTS-FA.md) is in place. After any rebuild, check `git diff --stat site/` for unexpected image losses.
- Local preview: `python3 -m http.server 8080 --directory site` → http://localhost:8080/

## Brand / design
- Font: Kalameh only (`site/assets/fonts/kalameh/*.woff2`, FaNum). Persian digits in Persian UI. Read `docs/persian-typography.md` before typography work.
- Brand teals: `#066163 #05686b #015F61 #0e7475 #087673`; mint backgrounds `#e8f3f3` / `#f3fafa`.
- No yellow or lime accents on teal. No blood or gore visuals. No mouse-move or cursor-follow effects.
- Three themes, light, dark and noir (purple), must all work on every page (`data-theme` on `<html>`, `localStorage["abadis-theme"]`, `?theme=` URL param). One toggle cycles them.
- Header is transparent in every theme; `.scrolled` only fades in an untinted blur; `.on-light` switches ink/logo to teal over light content (light theme).
- Footer cert area keeps ONLY the strip `site/assets/img/certs/abd-certs-768x119-1-copy.webp` (CE · ISO 13485:2016 · IMED).
- Main menu order (RTL): آشنایی با ما، محصولات، آخرین اخبار، لیست نمایندگان، توسعه پایدار، مقالات، ارتباط با ما، محاسبه‌گر.

## Content
- Product and page copy are verbatim from abadis-med.com. Never invent, rewrite or "improve" copy, specs, numbers, names or certificates.
- Sources, in order: live site (https may fail from some networks, but `http://abadis-med.com/wp-content/uploads/...` and the WP REST API `http://abadis-med.com/wp-json/wp/v2/...` work over plain http; also `/en/wp-json/` and `/arabic/wp-json/`), then the Wayback Machine (`https://web.archive.org/web/2026id_/<url>`).
- Every page keeps `<meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow">` until the launch task (prompt 6) removes it deliberately.

## Working style
- Do only the task asked. Don't refactor unrelated code. Keep replies short; report what changed, commit SHA, and anything left open.
- Ask before adding new paid services, accounts, fonts or large dependencies.
